---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Timeline from '../components/Timeline.astro';
import { tracks, totalNotes, totalWeeks } from '../data/roadmap';

const ready = tracks.flatMap((t) => t.notes).filter((n) => n.ready).length;
---

<Base title="Home">
  <div class="prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">A {totalWeeks}-week path · {totalNotes} notes · 5 projects</p>
    <h1>AI Engineer Notes</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      From “what is a vector?” to designing LLM systems in an interview. Every idea is explained simply first, then
      precisely, then in words you can say out loud, and then practised until it sticks.
    </p>

    <p>
      These notes assume no AI background and no more math than school algebra. Each one starts with an everyday
      explanation, shows the idea as a picture, then gives the exact technical terms, the math and the code. It ends
      with a model interview answer, practice questions and a revision card.
    </p>
    <p>
      Start with the <a href="/roadmap/">roadmap</a> to see what to study each week, use the
      <a href="/practice/">practice page</a> for the drills, and check the <a href="/projects/">projects</a> you will
      build alongside. {ready} of {totalNotes} <a href="/notes/">notes</a> are written so far.
    </p>

    <Timeline />

    <h2>The nine tracks</h2>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Track</th><th>When</th><th>Notes</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {
            tracks.map((track) => (
              <tr>
                <td>
                  <a href={`/notes/#${track.id}`}>
                    {track.number}. {track.title}
                  </a>
                </td>
                <td>{track.weeks}</td>
                <td>{track.notes.length}</td>
              </tr>
            ))
          }
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
